# Lab 1 — Build and Package a Java Application with Maven

## Objective
Build, test, package, and run the Calculator Java application using Maven.

## Prerequisites
- Java JDK (prefer Java 17)
- Apache Maven
- Git

## Source code
```bash
git clone https://github.com/Ibrahim-Adel15/CalculatorMavenApp.git
cd CalculatorMavenApp
```

## 1. Verify the tools
```bash
java -version
javac -version
mvn -version
```

## 2. Run unit tests
```bash
mvn test
```
Expected: Maven finishes with `BUILD SUCCESS`. If tests fail, read the first test failure in the output before proceeding.

## 3. Package the application
```bash
mvn package
```

## 4. Run the application
First inspect the JAR manifest and repository instructions if the JAR does not run:
```bash
java -jar target/calculator.jar
```
## 5. Verify
Use the application's prompts and enter sample values. Confirm the calculator returns the expected result. Record the commands, test result, and artifact name.


